<section class="mkt-hero">
  <div>
    <h1>Send every task to the right worker.</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      fm-steer routes work by difficulty, tracks token spend per account, and shows its reasons. One CLI, one portal, no guessing.
    </p>
    <div class="mkt-cta">
      <.link href={~p"/steer#install"} class="btn btn-primary">Install fm-steer</.link>
      <.link href={~p"/steer#routing"} class="btn btn-quiet">How routing works</.link>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="term" role="img" aria-label="Example fm-steer route and usage output">
    <div><span class="p">$</span> fm-steer route "fix the failing test"</div>
    <div>harness codex</div>
    <div>model GPT-6-Astra (gpt-6-astra)</div>
    <div>effort medium</div>
    <div><span class="c">- codex wins on quality x cost x latency</span></div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div><span class="p">$</span> fm-steer usage</div>
    <div>openrouter&nbsp;&nbsp;captain&nbsp;&nbsp;100.00&nbsp;&nbsp;25.00&nbsp;&nbsp;75.00&nbsp;&nbsp;ok</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section" id="routing">
  <h2>Routing with reasons attached</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    The portal classifies each task on six axes, filters the fleet capability
    matrix on hard constraints, and picks the cheapest lane that qualifies.
    Every answer names its harness, model, effort, and why.
  </p>
  <div class="flow">
    <div>
      <h3>Classify</h3>
      <p>Kind, ambiguity, blast radius, citations, risk, and whether live web is required. A rater agent can override any axis.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Filter</h3>
      <p>Lanes that miss a constraint drop out with a note. Artificial Analysis only annotates the surviving lane; it never changes it.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Pick</h3>
      <p>Cheapest qualifier wins, ties break on latency. Higher ambiguity, blast radius, or risk raises the effort and the model with it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section" id="usage">
  <h2>Spend you can see</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    One ledger per tenant for every provider account: allowance, used,
    remaining, and runway from real burn rate. Unknown allowances stay
    unknown. Nothing is guessed.
  </p>
  <table class="sample-table" aria-label="Sample usage ledger">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Account</th><th>Used</th><th>Remaining</th><th>Status</th><th>Runway</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>openrouter / captain</td>
        <td class="num">25.00 / 100.00 USD</td>
        <td class="num">75.00</td>
        <td>ok</td>
        <td class="num">14.0d</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>anthropic / direct</td>
        <td class="num">82.10 / 100.00 USD</td>
        <td class="num">17.90</td>
        <td>low</td>
        <td class="num">3.2d</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0;">Sample rows. Lower spend priority burns first. Every account is fed by posted readings.</p>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section" id="commands">
  <h2>Four verbs</h2>
  <p class="lede">Device code login once. Everything after that is one command.</p>
  <div class="cmd-grid">
    <div>
      <h3>Auth and inbox</h3>
      <pre>fm-steer auth login
fm-steer inbox put --task fm-port --body "hello"
fm-steer inbox next --task fm-port</pre>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Route and usage</h3>
      <pre>fm-steer route "deploy the portal to production"
fm-steer usage
fm-steer usage --json</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section" id="docs">
  <h2>Docs</h2>
  <p class="lede">Short pages for operators and for agents calling the API.</p>
  <div class="doc-rows">
    <.link navigate={~p"/steer/docs/fm-steer"}>
      <span><strong>fm-steer CLI</strong><p>Install, auth, inbox, route, and usage commands.</p></span>
      <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span>
    </.link>
    <.link navigate={~p"/steer/docs/routing"}>
      <span><strong>Routing</strong><p>Axes, capability matrix, provider intel, eval set, API.</p></span>
      <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span>
    </.link>
    <.link navigate={~p"/steer/docs/usage"}>
      <span><strong>Usage and billing</strong><p>Accounts, windows, spend priority, runway.</p></span>
      <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span>
    </.link>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section" id="install">
  <h2>Install</h2>
  <p class="lede">Build from this repo. Point at your portal. Log in once.</p>
  <div class="term" role="img" aria-label="Example fm-steer install commands">
    <div><span class="p">$</span> go build -o fm-steer ./cmd/fm-steer</div>
    <div><span class="p">$</span> export FIRSTMATE_INSTANCE=http://localhost:4000</div>
    <div><span class="p">$</span> fm-steer auth login</div>
  </div>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0;">Credentials land at $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fm-steer/credentials.json with mode 0600. The CLI only calls the portal API, so your tenant follows your login.</p>
</section>
